{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "RAK3172-T-9-SM-I",
 "kind": "wireless_module",
 "manufacturer": "RAKwireless",
 "title": "RAK3172 WisDuo: LoRaWAN and LoRa P2P sub-GHz module on the STM32WLE5CC",
 "source": {
  "revision": "Last updated 9/19/2023",
  "pages": 9
 },
 "summary": "A 15.5 × 15 mm surface-mount LPWAN module built on the STM32WLE5CCU6, which pairs an Arm Cortex-M4 with a sub-GHz LoRa radio, 256 kB of flash with ECC and 64 kB of RAM. It runs LoRaWAN 1.0.3 Classes A, B and C with OTAA or ABP join, or LoRa point-to-point, and is driven by AT commands over UART or programmed with the RUI3 API in Arduino. It comes in a low-band (EU433, CN470) and a high-band (EU868 up to AS923) build, runs from 2.0 to 3.6 V and sleeps at 1.69 µA. The -T version carries a TCXO and is rated -40 to 85 °C, the standard one -20 to 85 °C.",
