 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Inside the module",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The STM32WLE5CCU6 reaches its RF subsystem over SUBGHZSPI, a dedicated internal SPI interface."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Block diagram",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The STM32WLE5Cx runs from a 32.768 kHz crystal and a 32 MHz crystal. Its RF path goes through an RF switch to the IPEX connector, with a branch to the RF pad. UART, I2C, ADC, GPIO, SPI and 3V3 are brought out of the module."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Band versions",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The module is built for one of two radio bands. RAK3172(L) covers the low band (EU433 and CN470); RAK3172(H) covers the high band (EU868, US915, AU915, KR920, AS923-1/2/3/4, IN865 and RU864). Pin 27, PB12, is pulled to the supply through 10 kΩ on the high-band build and to ground on the low-band build."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature and oscillator versions",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "RAK3172 is rated -20 to 85 °C. RAK3172-T, fitted with a TCXO, is rated -40 to 85 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Certification versions",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two certified builds exist: one marked CE and UKCA, the other marked FCC, IC and RCM."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Antenna connection",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "One build has an IPEX connector on the module; the other brings the antenna out on the RF pad, pin 12. With the RF pad, no layer of the host board carries ground plane under the RF trace; stray capacitance from it degrades the RF signal level."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pin-compatible part",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "RAK11720 fits the same footprint and adds BLE 5.0, with extra ground pads and a BLE antenna port."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Firmware",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Both band builds run the same RUI3 firmware, which detects which build it is on. The .bin image holds the application alone and is loaded with the RAK DFU Tool; the .hex image holds bootloader and application and is loaded with STM32CubeProgrammer, which wipes all stored configuration. Firmware is loaded over UART2 (pins 1 and 2) at a default 115200 baud. The module enters boot mode by itself when loaded from RAK DFU Tool or WisToolBox; otherwise the AT+BOOT command starts the bootloader."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Older firmware",
   "page": 8,
   "text": "Some modules shipped with firmware v1.0.4 or earlier, which predates RUI3, defaults to 9600 baud and uses an AT command set that differs in a few commands from RUI3's."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Footprint",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "The land pattern uses 0.7 mm wide pads on a 1.0 mm pitch, each 1.8 mm long and reaching 0.8 mm beyond the module outline; the pattern spans 16.6 mm across the 15.0 mm side."
  }
 ],
